# Frontend (`apps/web`)

Next.js App Router, React, TanStack Form + Query, Better Auth **client** (`lib/auth` → Hono `/api/auth/*`), Tailwind CSS **v4**, shadcn/base-nova under `components/ui/`.

Placement: **`layering`** + **`structure`**.

## Naming

Feature/component files: `kebab-case` (`sign-in-form.tsx`); PascalCase exports. Routes: `page.tsx` / `layout.tsx`.

## TypeScript

- Extend `../../tsconfig.base.json`; Next options (`jsx`/`bundler`/`plugins`/`paths` `@/*`) local

## Layout

| Layer | Location | Pattern |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Routes | `app/**` | thin pages; compose features |
| Features | `features/**` | domain UI, forms, feature hooks |
| Design system | `components/ui/` | shadcn atoms only |
| Shared non-feature UI | `components/` | providers/shell |
| Auth client | `lib/auth/` | `better-auth/react` client; BA session cookie via `/api/auth/*` proxy |
| Server state | `lib/query/` | TanStack Query |
| Client UI state | `stores/` | Zustand UI-only (create when needed) |
| Validation | `lib/validations/` | form Zod; auth bounds from `@gloaming/shared/auth/policy` |
| Constants | `constants/` | literals used 2+ times |
| Assets | `public/` | optional (`.gitkeep` OK) |

- Prefer existing `components/ui/`; shadcn CLI; ask before editing `components/ui/**` source
- Zustand: UI-only — never API/server SoT (`layering`)

### Feature page composition (anti–god component)

Prefer **compose many focused components** over one 700–1000 line page module.

| Rule | Detail |
| --- | --- |
| Thin route | `app/**/page.tsx` only passes params / renders a feature entry |
| Page = orchestrator | `*-page.tsx` owns data load, empty/error gates, layout chrome; delegates UI surfaces |
| Colocate siblings | Page-owned pieces live next to the page under `features/<domain>/` (same dir), not in a catch-all `components/` |
| Size ceiling | Soft ~300–400 lines; hard split at **>500** — see `structure` Feature UI size ceiling |
| Isolation | Keep selection state, chat/rail state, form editor state in their owning child; parent passes props / callbacks |
| When to split vs wait | Split structure **before** wiring the next real API into a megacomponent — do not wait for “full real data” to carve boundaries |
| Not this rule | Stub/mock honesty, data-flow bugs, and `formatXApiError = formatApiError` aliases — fix those separately; splitting alone does not fix them |

Example shape:

```text
features/learn/
  learn-room-page.tsx      # query + chrome + compose
  learn-article-reader.tsx # body + selection popover
  learn-help-rail.tsx      # assist rail
  learn-api.ts
```

## Styling

Tailwind v4 (`@import "tailwindcss"`); semantic tokens over raw colors.

### UI implementation ladder (aesthetics first)

Product UI must look like Gloaming (`DESIGN.md`) first; atoms are a means, not the goal.

1. Prefer **shadcn** atoms in `components/ui/` (add via CLI: `pnpm exec shadcn add …` from `apps/web`). Use variants/props first.
2. Polish with **Tailwind `className`** on those atoms when defaults fall short.
3. Compose atoms + light structural markup if still short.
4. **Last resort:** native DOM + Tailwind when no suitable atom exists.

Do not hand-roll a parallel control system. Do not ship “used shadcn but ugly/default tooling” UIs.

**System UI language:** Chinese for labels, nav, empty states, toasts, placeholders. Content field *values* may be EN/ZH.

**Base UI gotchas:** `Button` + `Link` → `nativeButton={false}`. Tabs active → `data-active`. Toggle pressed → `data-pressed`. Segmented filters: prefer `Tabs`; override list `h-8` with `h-auto` and pad triggers — avoid fixed-height fights.

## Auth

Soft UX only: cookie presence in `proxy.ts` (`better-auth.session_token` / `__Secure-…`), session + **401 → sign-in** in the client.
**Real auth** is Better Auth on `apps/backend` (`auth.api.getSession` / `requireAuth`) — not the Next soft gate.
`/admin/**` must check session `user.role` with `@gloaming/shared/auth/policy` before rendering admin content; hiding nav links is UX only, not authorization.
Any backend-backed admin data must also be protected by Hono `requireAdmin`; never rely on `proxy.ts` or client checks as the security boundary.
`DELETE /api/auth/logout` is a Next handler so HttpOnly BA session cookie(s) clear on this origin, then Hono `sign-out`.
Password/username bounds from `@gloaming/shared/auth/policy` — do not re-declare in web Zod.

## Prototype / stub UI

Admin/content screens backed by static arrays, mock data, or UI-only toasts must be explicitly labeled as prototype/stub in both source comments and user-facing Chinese copy. Do not imply persistence, publishing, CMS sync, or backend integration until the Hono content module exists.
